# Normalize all text to LF in the repository.
#
# The vendored Appian skill (iadc-advisor/skills/appian/) arrived with CRLF while
# its upstream (github.com/appian/dev-mcp-skills) uses LF. Left alone, every file
# reads as fully changed on a `git subtree pull`, burying real conflicts in
# line-ending noise. See docs/vendored-appian-skill.md.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The SessionStart hook must be LF: CRLF breaks a shebang script on Linux and in
# Git-for-Windows bash. hooks/session-start is extensionless (ADR 0012) so *.sh no longer
# matches it — named explicitly so the rule survives that rename. A gitattributes pattern that
# contains a slash is anchored to this file's own directory (the repo root), not matched at any
# depth, so the path has to be given in full from here: iadc-advisor/hooks/session-start, not
# hooks/session-start. *.sh is kept for any future shell script that does carry the extension.
*.sh text eol=lf
iadc-advisor/hooks/session-start text eol=lf

# run-hook.cmd is a polyglot (docs/hooks-dispatcher.md): the same bytes are read by bash and by
# cmd.exe. A CRLF copy dies with `line N: $'\r': command not found`, exit 127, zero output — the
# bash half chokes on a carriage return cmd.exe would silently tolerate.
*.cmd text eol=lf
